  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RUSI Analysing Organised Crime &#x2013; Terrorism Linkages from the Ground Up (KEN, MOZ, NGA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing an advanced evidence base through in-depth empirical research and making it available to inform current efforts to counter transnational organised crime and terrorism in Kenya, Mozambique and Nigeria.

The planned main products and/or services of the Project are (Outputs):
&#x2022;	A detailed strategic assessment based on a review of existing literature, providing a clear up-to date picture of the existing knowledge of the TOC-terror interface, the level of local input into this evidence base and the nature of existing responses.
&#x2022;	New primary research on lived experience of the TOC-terror interface and the record of existing responses, providing an enhanced evidence base and opportunity to increase local analytical capabilities.
&#x2022;	Publication of findings in three Operational Papers presenting policy focused recommendations and one Occasional Paper on best-practises in bottom-up research.
&#x2022;	Targeted engagement with local, national and global stakeholders through formal dialogues and a three-part launch series.

Local partners: 
Kenya: Centre for Human Rights and Policy Studies (CHRIPS)
Mozambique: Centre for Democracy and Development (CDD)   
Nigeria: Conciliation Resources (CR)</narrative>
  </description>
